## How to Run

```bash
# 1. Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/cnn-bilstm-stress-detection.git
cd cnn-bilstm-stress-detection

# 2. Install dependencies
pip install numpy pandas scikit-learn tensorflow matplotlib seaborn

# 3. Place the WESAD dataset in the data/ folder

# 4. Open and run the notebook
jupyter notebook notebooks/stress_detection.ipynb
```

You can also upload the notebook to Google Colab and run all cells.

## Key Highlights

- End-to-end single-stage framework with no manual feature engineering
- Captures both spatial (CNN) and temporal (Bi-LSTM) patterns
- Balanced performance across all three classes
- Evaluated with accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score, MSE, MAE, RMSE, confusion matrix, and ROC-AUC

## Future Work

- Test with real-time data from commercial smartwatches
- Build personalized models for individual users
- Add attention mechanisms and improve the Amusement class

